Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:33:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 26/32] metal: chunk rows + group planes, exact beyond-horizon
 nm1

Memory: one inversion call can hold 270M row-channels; materialising
per-item vectors for all of them (~45 GB of accumulate copies across
201 planes) stalls the machine. Process row chunks (<=1M items) sharing
one global layout, plane groups capped at 256 MB; dirty accumulates
with +=, corrections run once. Identical results (lwa50k 1.43e-08
before and after).

Correctness (wide-field): ducc0's beyond-horizon nm1 is
-sqrt(sum-1)-1, not -sqrt(sum)-1; also port its exact extrema scan
(xext/yext, sqrt(1-tmp)-1 inside). Narrow-field was inside the horizon
and never saw it; full-sky LWA was 3.7e-03, now 1.5e-08 on the 50k
subset. Wide synthetic (pixel-scale 10): 0.025 -> 1.5e-07.

